WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.954
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambodia Grade nine English.

2
00:00:06.254 --> 00:00:09.710
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:15.797
Unit three: Present Perfect. Today you will connect the past with the present using have and has.

4
00:00:16.097 --> 00:00:18.865
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.451
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.317 --> 00:00:25.190
Already.

7
00:00:26.183 --> 00:00:28.032
Already means before now.

8
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:30.059
I have already eaten.

9
00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:33.012
Your turn. Say: Already.

10
00:00:35.867 --> 00:00:36.868
Already.

11
00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:38.386
Yet.

12
00:00:39.383 --> 00:00:41.870
Yet means until now (in questions and negatives).

13
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:43.798
Have you finished yet?

14
00:00:44.383 --> 00:00:46.629
Your turn. Say: Yet.

15
00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.212
Yet.

16
00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:51.812
Just.

17
00:00:52.817 --> 00:00:55.002
Just means a very short time ago.

18
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:56.896
She has just left.

19
00:00:57.483 --> 00:00:59.683
Your turn. Say: Just.

20
00:01:02.533 --> 00:01:03.465
Just.

21
00:01:04.217 --> 00:01:04.997
Ever.

22
00:01:05.983 --> 00:01:08.041
Ever means at any time in your life.

23
00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:10.197
Have you ever been to Siem Reap?

24
00:01:10.783 --> 00:01:13.018
Your turn. Say: Ever.

25
00:01:15.867 --> 00:01:16.670
Ever.

26
00:01:17.417 --> 00:01:18.220
Never.

27
00:01:19.217 --> 00:01:21.019
Never means not at any time.

28
00:01:21.617 --> 00:01:23.349
I have never seen snow.

29
00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.405
Your turn. Say: Never.

30
00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:30.036
Never.

31
00:01:30.783 --> 00:01:31.448
For.

32
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:34.310
For means a period of time.

33
00:01:34.917 --> 00:01:36.742
I have lived here for five years.

34
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:39.584
Your turn. Say: For.

35
00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:43.191
For.

36
00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:44.812
Since.

37
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:47.758
Since means from a point in time.

38
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:51.255
I have studied English since 2022.

39
00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.235
Your turn. Say: Since.

40
00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.066
Since.

41
00:01:58.817 --> 00:02:00.154
Past participle.

42
00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:04.078
Past participle means the third form of the verb.

43
00:02:04.683 --> 00:02:07.089
Eaten is the past participle of eat.

44
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:10.475
Your turn. Say: Past participle.

45
00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.344
Past participle.

46
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.912
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:23.179
Visal, when do we use the present perfect?

48
00:02:24.283 --> 00:02:36.456
We use have or has plus the past participle to talk about experiences, recent actions and situations that continue to now. For example, I have visited Angkor Wat.

49
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.155
How do for and since differ?

50
00:02:40.250 --> 00:02:53.142
We use for with a period of time, such as for three years, and since with a starting point, such as since 2021. Both are used with the present perfect.

51
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.145
What about already, yet and just?

52
00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:07.161
Already and just go before the past participle. Yet goes at the end of questions and negatives: Have you finished yet? I haven't finished yet.

53
00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.847
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:10.683 --> 00:03:15.098
Grammar focus: Present perfect: have and has plus past participle.

55
00:03:15.398 --> 00:03:16.631
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.317 --> 00:03:19.374
I have lived here for five years.

57
00:03:20.283 --> 00:03:22.225
She has just finished her homework.

58
00:03:23.167 --> 00:03:32.065
Use have or has plus the past participle for experience and for situations that continue to now. For means a period, since means a starting point.

59
00:03:32.817 --> 00:03:36.758
Be careful! Don't say: I live here since 2020.

60
00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.162
Say: I have lived here since 2020.

61
00:03:42.462 --> 00:03:44.543
Use present perfect with since.

62
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:48.137
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:48.933 --> 00:03:50.294
A Long Friendship.

64
00:03:50.594 --> 00:03:53.592
Rithy and Vanna have been friends since primary school.

65
00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.600
They have known each other for eight years.

66
00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:00.180
They have never argued about anything serious.

67
00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.816
Vanna has just joined the school football team.

68
00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:08.355
Rithy hasn't joined yet, but he has already bought his uniform.

69
00:04:09.467 --> 00:04:13.329
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:14.183 --> 00:04:16.369
I blank in Phnom Penh for ten years.

71
00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:20.264
A, have lived. B, lived. C, am living.

72
00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.765
The answer is A: have lived.

73
00:04:26.917 --> 00:04:29.950
She has studied English blank 2022.

74
00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:33.311
A, during. B, since. C, for.

75
00:04:36.867 --> 00:04:39.075
The answer is B: since.

76
00:04:40.217 --> 00:04:41.589
Have you finished blank?

77
00:04:41.889 --> 00:04:44.858
A, already. B, just. C, yet.

78
00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:50.179
The answer is C: yet.

79
00:04:51.317 --> 00:04:53.479
How long have the friends known each other?

80
00:04:53.779 --> 00:04:57.676
A, eight years. B, two years. C, a week.

81
00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.198
The answer is A: eight years.

82
00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:06.466
The past participle of 'eat' is blank.

83
00:05:06.766 --> 00:05:09.827
A, eating. B, eaten. C, ate.

84
00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.088
The answer is B: eaten.

85
00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:19.185
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.655
What have you done this week?

87
00:05:30.450 --> 00:05:31.881
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.181 --> 00:05:44.240
This week I have finished two projects and I have studied for my English test. I have also helped my mother at home. I haven't visited my friends yet, but I plan to see them on Sunday.

89
00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:46.214
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:47.117 --> 00:05:53.206
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and present perfect: have and has plus past participle.

91
00:05:53.506 --> 00:05:57.493
Today's value is reflection. Think about what you learned and how you grew.

92
00:05:57.793 --> 00:06:00.155
See you in Unit four. Goodbye!

93
00:06:00.455 --> 00:06:03.015
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

